**`/bench/repo/web/src/connect.ts`**

All eight service clients are created and exported from that one file. A single shared `createConnectTransport` is configured against the page origin using the binary wire format, a credentials-aware `fetch`, and an auth interceptor, then each client is built on top of it:

```184:194:/bench/repo/web/src/connect.ts
const transport = createConnectTransport({
  baseUrl: window.location.origin,
  useBinaryFormat: true,
  fetch: fetchWithCredentials,
  interceptors: [authInterceptor],
});

// Core service clients
export const instanceServiceClient = createClient(InstanceService, transport);
export const authServiceClient = createClient(AuthService, transport);
export const userServiceClient = createClient(UserService, transport);
```

The exports continue through `memoServiceClient`, `attachmentServiceClient`, `aiServiceClient`, `shortcutServiceClient`, and `identityProviderServiceClient` at lines 197–203, matching the eight backend services one-to-one.

The same file also defines a second, separate transport at line 65 with its own `refreshAuthClient` (line 72). That one deliberately skips the auth interceptor so token-refresh calls can't recurse into the interceptor that triggers them.
